The third age brought darkness to the dungeon.
The torches guttered and died one by one,
until only a faint glow remained in the deepest rooms.

The archivists grew fewer with each passing year,
and the great library fell into neglect.
Dust gathered on the shelves, and cobwebs
draped themselves across the forgotten tomes.

Yet the runes endured, patient and silent,
waiting for a seeker worthy of their power.

